# TCB production-path panic-surface ratchet. Read by
# scripts/check_tcb_panic_freedom.sh; the gate FAILS if the live count exceeds
# the number below. Ratchet DOWN only. Whoever moves it records why here.
#
# 2026-07-24 — 180 -> 297. Two independent things were wrong at once.
#
#   Measurement. The 180 was produced by a raw line grep that counted comment
#   prose and string-literal text as panic sites. In the TCB that is not a
#   rounding error: vcgen and trust_verify DOCUMENT the panicking code they
#   reason about, so 107 of the 404 the old counter reported at this commit
#   were sentences, not statements — and the old number could be lowered by
#   deleting explanations. The counter now erases comments and literal
#   contents and drops every `#[cfg(test)]` item whole before matching. Its
#   answer at the 2026-06-23 snapshot commit (8a653fe5cb) is 167, which lands
#   on the hand-classified "real code" table in reports/tcb-hardening-audit.md
#   (unwrap 15 = 15, unreachable 47 vs 48); the 180 never matched even its own
#   counter, which read 201 on that tree.
#
#   Drift. Measured consistently, the code surface still grew 167 -> 297 over
#   the ~3700 commits since the snapshot, concentrated in trust-types (+33),
#   trust-cg-bridge (+26), trust-vcgen (+20), trust_verify (+16). The gate was
#   red that whole time, so it caught none of it. 297 is the honest count
#   today, not an acceptable one: it is a burn-down backlog, and the ratchet
#   works again from here. Reproduce it from a clean checkout at d9616037e0:
#   scripts/check_tcb_panic_freedom.sh --print.
# 2026-07-25: 297 -> 283. `chc::binop_to_formula` deleted — it was a thin
# panicking wrapper (`unwrap_or_else(|err| panic!(...))`) over the fallible
# `try_binop_to_formula`, sitting in the verification path. It had NO production
# callers left: trust-transval had already migrated with a comment saying
# "rather than panicking inside chc::binop_to_formula -- the verifier core", and
# the two remaining in-crate sites now pass the Result straight through their
# match arms. Test call sites unwrap, which is where unwrapping belongs.
283
